<title>USA: Ocean City, Md., mayor says won't sign tax hike.</title>
<headline>Ocean City, Md., mayor says won't sign tax hike.</headline>
<dateline>OCEAN CITY, Md. 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The mayor of Ocean City, Md., said he would not sign the city council's fiscal 1998 budget because it includes a one-cent property tax increase.</p>
<p>Mayor Jim Mathias said the present tax rate is high enough. The city is required to approve a final budget by July 1.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
